{
  "$comment": "Cases for both manifest checkers -- the reference in Go (tools/internal/formats) and Clack's own in the browser (src/manifest.ts) -- so the two cannot drift apart. Each of \"cases\" applies its edits to schema/examples/manifest.json (a JSON Pointer to the value to set; null removes it; \"\" replaces the whole document) and says where the errors must be: one place, a list of places, or null for a manifest that must be accepted. A refused case must have an error at each place and nowhere else. Each of \"raw\" is a whole file, as base64 bytes, for what only shows in the bytes, and says only whether it is accepted.",
